{# ============================================================ HERO
   Full-bleed photo layer (absolute, right-biased, no frame) with text
   overlaid — rebuilt 2026-08-24 v2 after side-by-side comparison against the
   reference showed the first pass reading as a boxed/contained photo panel
   with too much vertical padding, not the reference's edge-to-edge, tightly
   composed atmosphere. This version: photo is an absolute layer spanning the
   full section height (visible behind the fixed nav at the very top, same
   as the reference), no rounded frame, a wide gradient blend into paper
   instead of a hard edge, and a shorter, denser hero overall.
   Reuses existing site infrastructure rather than inventing new systems —
   the [data-hero-in] GSAP stagger (main.js) for entrance, the same
   overscan-then-transform parallax pattern already used on .facet-field,
   and the existing btn-primary/btn-ghost component classes.
   Eyebrow pill is back, deliberately overriding the earlier Impeccable-driven
   removal — explicit ask this round.
   Every element renders fully visible in plain HTML/CSS first; GSAP only
   choreographs entrance once it has actually loaded (see main.js comment). #}
<section class="relative bg-paper overflow-hidden">
  {# Photo layer — absolute, right-biased, no rounding, no contained box.
     Starts BELOW the fixed nav (top-20/80px — the nav bar's resting-state
     bottom edge measures 69.5px now that the header defaults to a flush
     full-width bar rather than a floating pill, so this is a tight,
     deliberate ~10px margin below that, not a guess) rather than spanning
     the section's full height behind it. Earlier versions let the photo
     extend behind the nav for a more edge-to-edge look, but that meant
     anything near the top of the source photo — specifically the thrown
     caps — could end up partly hidden under the nav depending on viewport
     size, and no amount of crop tuning fixed it reliably at every size.
     Starting below the nav guarantees zero overlap regardless of viewport,
     full stop. #}
  <div class="absolute right-0 top-20 bottom-0 w-full lg:w-[58%] overflow-hidden">
    {# The parallax target is this inner, overscanned (-6% top/bottom)
       wrapper — GSAP moves it within the statically sized, overflow-hidden
       layer so scrolling never exposes a gap (same technique as .facet-field).
       object-position biased right-of-frame: the source photo has an
       "admizz" watermark baked into its top-left corner (known defect,
       docs/RESUME-PROMPT.md) — this crop keeps it out of view without
       needing a re-exported asset. #}
    <div class="hero-photo-parallax absolute -inset-y-[2%] inset-x-0 [&_picture]:contents [&_img]:absolute [&_img]:inset-0 [&_img]:h-full [&_img]:w-full [&_img]:object-cover [&_img]:object-[60%_0%] [&_img]:scale-110">
      {% imageEager "src/assets/images/insights/global-opportunities.jpg", "Graduates celebrating, caps thrown in the air", "(min-width: 1024px) 64vw, 100vw" %}
    </div>
    {# Brand-shape watermark — the logo mark's chevron silhouette, simplified
       to a single flat translucent band and layered ON TOP of the photo.
       Blurred: the previous crisp-edged version rendered as a visible hard
       diagonal seam cutting across the faces/arms — looked like a rendering
       bug, not a brand shape. The reference's version reads as soft ambient
       light, not a cut geometric edge, so a real blur (not just low opacity)
       is what actually fixes it. #}
    <svg class="absolute left-1/2 top-[3%] -translate-x-1/2 w-[105%] max-w-[820px] h-auto pointer-events-none blur-2xl" viewBox="0 0 400 260" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" aria-hidden="true">
      <path d="M200,5 L340,105 L280,105 L200,50 L120,105 L60,105 Z" fill="#FFFFFF" opacity="0.18"/>
      <path d="M200,120 L390,250 L305,250 L200,175 L95,250 L10,250 Z" fill="#FFFFFF" opacity="0.15"/>
    </svg>
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-navy-deep/18 via-transparent to-transparent"></div>
    {# Atmospheric blend into the paper ground — width-controlled via Tailwind's
       gradient stop positions. Narrowed twice now (first pass: via-75%/to-90%;
       this pass: via-38%/to-58%) so most of the photo stays fully saturated —
       only enough coverage to keep the text column clean, not a wash across
       the whole frame. #}
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-r from-paper from-0% via-paper/65 via-22% to-transparent to-58% lg:to-50%"></div>
    {# Top-edge blend — the photo's left edge already fades into the paper
       column (above); the top edge didn't, so where the nav's protective
       gap (see the top-20 comment above) sits over paper it was invisible,
       but the exact same gap sitting over the photo read as a hard, visible
       seam — one gap, two different results depending on contrast. This
       fades the photo's own top ~64px from paper down to fully transparent,
       so it emerges out of the ground the same way the left edge already
       does, rather than starting with a flat line. #}
    <div class="absolute inset-x-0 top-0 h-16 bg-gradient-to-b from-paper to-transparent"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="shell relative pt-28 pb-3 md:pt-28 md:pb-4">
    <div class="min-h-[320px] md:min-h-[380px] lg:min-h-[430px] flex items-center">
      <div class="relative z-10 max-w-xl">
        {# Dot-grid globe motif, anchored to THIS text column (not the raw
           section) — the earlier version was positioned against the
           full-width section, so on wide viewports the shell centers with a
           growing left margin and the circle rendered mostly off-screen,
           clipped to a meaningless sliver instead of a visible globe. #}
        <svg class="absolute -left-16 -top-14 w-[560px] h-[560px] opacity-[0.16] pointer-events-none hidden lg:block -z-10" viewBox="0 0 560 560" aria-hidden="true">
          <defs>
            <pattern id="hero-dots" width="20" height="20" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
              <circle cx="1.5" cy="1.5" r="1.5" fill="#0B0F69"/>
            </pattern>
            <clipPath id="hero-dots-circle"><circle cx="280" cy="280" r="280"/></clipPath>
          </defs>
          <rect width="560" height="560" fill="url(#hero-dots)" clip-path="url(#hero-dots-circle)"/>
        </svg>

        <span class="eyebrow-pill" data-hero-in>
          <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 bg-navy"></span>
          Shaping futures. Building possibilities.
        </span>

        {# Hero-scoped heading size, smaller than the shared .text-display-1
           token — that clamp scales to 96px on real desktop widths, and four
           wrapped lines at that size alone ate ~370px, which is what forced
           scrolling on shorter real browser windows. This keeps the same
           fluid/responsive behavior, just with a lower ceiling. #}
        <h1 class="mt-4 max-w-[680px] font-display font-light text-[clamp(1.85rem,1.25rem+2.5vw,3.4rem)] leading-[1.08] text-ink" data-hero-in>
          Transforming education and careers, <em class="italic text-navy font-book">globally.</em>
        </h1>

        <p class="mt-3 text-body-lg text-ink-muted max-w-measure-tight" data-hero-in>
          {{ site.description }}
        </p>

        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4" data-hero-in>
          <a href="#ventures" class="btn-primary group">
            Explore our ventures
            <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" class="transition-transform duration-press ease-signature group-hover:translate-x-0.5"><path d="M2 7h10M8 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          </a>
          <a href="/contact/" class="btn-ghost">Get in touch</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {# Real trust badge — Admizz Education's ICEF accreditation, independently
       verified against ICEF's public API (docs/01-AUDIT.md §2), not a claim
       taken from marketing copy. Anchored to the shell so it aligns with the
       curve below, positioned over the photo layer via z-index.
       Mobile fix: at the mobile min-h (320px) the CTA row sits near the
       bottom of this same shell, and this badge's bottom-0 previously
       landed right on top of it — clipping the primary "Explore our
       ventures" button. Below md it now sits in normal flow, after the
       CTAs; only at md+ (where the hero is tall enough for the badge to
       float clear of the button row) does it switch to absolute. #}
    <a
      href="https://accreditations.icef.com/certificate?id=c8a7212a-a25c-469f-8a7b-2b2f047e8c0c"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
      data-hero-in
      data-motion
      class="badge-float mt-6 md:mt-0 md:absolute md:bottom-0 right-gutter z-10 flex items-center gap-3 bg-white/95 backdrop-blur-sm shadow-xl border border-rule px-4 py-3 max-w-[240px] hover:shadow-2xl transition-shadow duration-press ease-signature"
    >
      <span class="shrink-0 w-9 h-9 bg-navy/10 flex items-center justify-center text-navy">
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 18 18" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M9 1.5l6 2.25v4c0 4-2.6 6.9-6 8.75-3.4-1.85-6-4.75-6-8.75v-4L9 1.5z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          <path d="M6.5 9l1.8 1.8L11.5 7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        </svg>
      </span>
      <span>
        <span class="block text-small font-medium text-ink">ICEF Certified Agency</span>
        <span class="block text-label text-ink-faint">Admizz Education &middot; Verified</span>
      </span>
    </a>
  </div>

  {# Curved cap transitioning the paper hero into the navy value band —
     SVG rather than clip-path here since it's bridging two stacked sections,
     not masking a single element; preserveAspectRatio="none" stretches it
     to full width, a standard, responsive technique for this shape.
     The seam bug: the SVG's fill edge anti-aliases against whatever sits
     behind the <svg> element itself, and the old 1px overlap (-mt-px)
     wasn't reliable across zoom levels/DPRs — at some scales a hairline of
     paper showed through as a visible line. Pulling the navy div up by a
     few real pixels (-mt-2) instead of one guarantees the overlap survives
     sub-pixel rounding at any scale. #}
  <div class="relative mt-4 md:mt-5">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 1440 140" preserveAspectRatio="none" class="block w-full h-[32px] md:h-[48px]" aria-hidden="true">
      <path d="M0,140 L0,45 C 480,135 900,-5 1440,80 L1440,140 Z" fill="#0B0F69"/>
    </svg>
    <div class="bg-navy-deep -mt-2 relative overflow-hidden">
      {# Soft diagonal light sweep — the reference's value band has real
         depth (a lighter-blue glow crossing the upper-left), not a flat
         single navy fill. A large, heavily blurred gradient shape reads as
         ambient light rather than a hard-edged decoration. #}
      <div class="absolute -top-1/2 -left-1/4 w-[75%] h-[220%] bg-gradient-to-br from-navy-soft/55 via-navy/20 to-transparent rotate-12 blur-3xl pointer-events-none" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="shell py-6 md:py-7 relative z-10">
        {# Real proof, not decoration — replaces the old "Global Reach / Student
           First / Future Ready" icon strip, which named zero facts. These are
           Admizz Education's own published figures (src/_data/stats.json,
           source: admizzeducation, status: draft), attributed explicitly —
           this is the group site reporting a venture's results, not claiming
           them as the whole group's. Caption pattern borrowed from scaler.com's
           stat block ("Based on the 2026 Scaler career transition assessment")
           — a number is only as credible as who it's attributed to. #}
        <span class="eyebrow-on-navy fade-up">Across Admizz Education</span>
        <div class="mt-5 grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 divide-y divide-navy-on-muted/15 md:divide-y-0 md:divide-x">
          {% for s in stats.headline %}
          <div class="py-4 md:py-0 md:px-8 first:pt-0 md:first:pl-0 last:pb-0 md:last:pr-0 fade-up" style="animation-delay:{{ loop.index0 * 90 }}ms">
            <span class="block font-display font-light text-h3 text-navy-on">{{ s.value }}</span>
            <span class="block mt-1 text-small text-navy-on-muted">{{ s.label }}</span>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
        <p class="mt-6 font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-navy-on-muted/70 fade-up">
          Figures published by Admizz Education, as of 2026
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ============================================================ 01 — WHAT ADMIZZ IS
   Positioning section — explains WHY the three businesses are one group,
   not just that they are. Doesn't exist as its own section pre-rebuild;
   was only implied in the hero subhead.

   2026-08-31 v3: rebuilt against the same reference mockup — the three
   venture "preview cards" now live INSIDE this section (photo, number,
   stage, name, one-liner sourced from the venture's own existing
   verticalLine field — nothing new written), plus a small vertical
   pathway diagram on the right, echoing the bigger Ecosystem-pathway
   section further down without duplicating it. This does NOT remove the
   bigger Prepare/Study/Work sticky section below — open question, still
   flagged, on whether that stays once this preview exists.

   2026-09-02: moved to come right after the hero (was second, after "The
   Shift") on explicit request — content and styling otherwise untouched,
   this is a pure section-order swap. The id="what-admizz-is" anchor and
   its own internal links are unaffected; "The Shift" section's own
   "Explore how we help" link no longer points here (see that section,
   now below, for why). #}
<section id="what-admizz-is" class="bg-paper-sunk py-section-sm border-b border-rule">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,22rem)_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-10 lg:gap-16">
      <div class="fade-up">
        <span class="eyebrow">What Admizz Is</span>
        <h2 class="mt-4 font-display font-light text-h1 text-ink max-w-[12ch] text-balance">
          One group. <em class="italic text-navy font-book">Three connected businesses.</em>
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="fade-up" style="animation-delay:90ms">
        <p class="text-body-lg text-ink-muted leading-relaxed max-w-measure">
          Admizz Institute, Admizz Education and Admizz Workforce Solutions each answer to a different market &mdash; test preparation, international admissions, and workforce development are not the same business, and we don&rsquo;t run them as one.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-body text-ink-muted leading-relaxed max-w-measure">
          What connects them is where they sit on the same line: a test score determines what a university application can achieve; a university decision shapes the career that follows it; a career runs on skills that keep changing after graduation. Most organizations serve one point on that line. Admizz was built to serve more than one of them, without pretending the three are interchangeable.
        </p>
        <a href="/ventures/" class="mt-6 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-small font-medium text-ink link-underline">
          Explore our businesses
          <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 7h10M8 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    {# Preview row: 3 venture cards + a mini pathway diagram alongside.
       All 3 photos are user-supplied, explicitly AI-generated images
       (against this project's own "no AI-look imagery" rule in
       docs/00-BRIEF.md §13 — overridden here on explicit instruction,
       same pattern as the ecosystem.jpg exceptions elsewhere, NOT a
       default for future sessions to repeat unprompted). #}
    {% set previewImages = {
      "institute": { file: "preview/institute-preview.jpg", alt: "Student wearing headphones, writing in a notebook" },
      "education": { file: "preview/education-preview.jpg", alt: "Student walking outside a university building with a backpack" },
      "workforce": { file: "preview/workforce-preview.jpg", alt: "Three colleagues talking in a modern office" }
    } %}
    {# 2026-09-02: cards used to sit in one shared .fade-up wrapper, so all
       three photos/labels popped in together as a single flat block --
       a design critique read this as "just content," no broadcast feel.
       Each card now gets its own GSAP-driven reveal (data-venture-preview-
       card, wired in main.js): index-staggered fade + a left-to-right
       clip-path wipe on the photo, same hide-then-reveal idiom as the
       hero/statement-band GSAP blocks elsewhere (visible by default in
       plain CSS; GSAP hides then reveals only once it has actually
       loaded). The mini pathway keeps its own simple .fade-up -- this
       treatment is for the cards specifically. #}
    <div class="mt-14 md:mt-16 grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_auto] gap-x-10 gap-y-10 items-start">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-x-8 gap-y-10">
        {% for v in ventures %}
        {% set img = previewImages[v.id] %}
        <div class="venture-preview-card" data-venture-preview-card>
          {# 2026-09-06: numbered service-card treatment (reference: SaleUnion) —
             index + stage combined into one compact mono line ("01 / PREPARE",
             was a large display numeral beside a separate mono label), photo
             moved up to lead the card (was name -> photo; now photo -> name),
             and the closing link upgraded from underlined text to a small
             solid pill button. Same data, same links, same photos throughout. #}
          <span class="font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-navy-soft">{{ v.index }} / {{ v.stage }}</span>
          <a href="{{ v.href if v.href != '#' else '/ventures/' }}" class="venture-preview-photo mt-3 block relative overflow-hidden bg-navy-deep aspect-[3/2]">
            <div class="absolute inset-0 [&_picture]:contents [&_picture]:block [&_picture]:h-full [&_img]:absolute [&_img]:inset-0 [&_img]:h-full [&_img]:w-full [&_img]:object-cover">
              {% image "src/assets/images/" + img.file, img.alt, "(min-width: 1024px) 22vw, (min-width: 640px) 30vw, 80vw" %}
            </div>
          </a>
          <h3 class="mt-4 font-display font-light text-h4 text-ink text-balance">{{ v.name }}</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-small text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">{{ v.verticalLine }}</p>
          <a href="/ventures/#record-{{ v.id }}" class="btn-card mt-4">
            Learn more
            <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 7h10M8 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          </a>
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>

      {# Mini pathway — echoes the bigger Ecosystem-pathway section further
         down (same 3 real stages, same gold-dot idiom) at a much smaller
         scale, as a compact index rather than a duplicate of that section. #}
      <div class="hidden lg:flex flex-col items-start gap-6 pl-8 border-l border-rule self-stretch justify-center fade-up" style="animation-delay:140ms">
        {% for v in ventures %}
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
          <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 bg-gold" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-faint">{{ v.stage }}</span>
        </div>
        {% if not loop.last %}<span class="w-px h-6 bg-rule ml-[3px]" aria-hidden="true"></span>{% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
        <span class="w-px h-6 bg-rule ml-[3px]" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
          <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 bg-navy-on-muted/50" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-faint">Opportunity</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ============================================================ 02 — THE SHIFT
   New 2026-08-31 (homepage-narrative rebuild). Originally the opening move
   of the homepage narrative, right after the hero: the world Admizz
   operates in, before Admizz itself. Moved to second position 2026-09-02
   (explicit request) — "What Admizz Is" now comes first instead. Content
   and styling below are otherwise unchanged; only the closing link's
   target changed (see that link's own comment).

   2026-08-31 v3: rebuilt against a reference mockup (user-supplied
   screenshot, same copy already written here, richer layout) — added the
   eyebrow, the numbered "what's changing" breakdown, a background world
   map, and a closing link.

   v4 CORRECTION: the first pass reused the hero's plain dot-grid CIRCLE —
   just a blob of dots, not a world map. Rebuilt with a real world outline
   (MIT-licensed, simplemaps.com) driving a CSS mask, but that produced a
   flat RECTANGLE (a map), not a globe.

   v5: tried a round, shaded globe (bleeding off the section's right edge)
   after v4's flat map wasn't right either.

   v6: v5's revert was misread as "delete the map" instead of "go back to
   the dotted world MAP version" — restored the flat dotted world map
   (world-map-dots, same as v4), positioned in the open space to the right
   of the two-column grid so it doesn't overlap the text now that the
   column widths/breakpoint are actually correct (see the placement fixes
   made to this section since v5). The tightened scale (narrower headline
   column, smaller list type/spacing) from v5 stays.

   v7: interactive globe (cobe) — superseded by v8, kept alive by moving
   it to the Academic Network section further down this page instead of
   deleting it (same markers, same JS hook, just relocated — see that
   section for why it fits better there: it's literally partner-country
   capitals, so it belongs next to the partner-network content, not here).

   v8 (2026-09-06): globe replaced with a short muted looping video of two
   people in conversation — reference: SaleUnion's "Our Impact" video
   panel. Section restructured from 2 narrow text columns (with the globe
   floating decoratively off to the side, xl+ only) into text-stack-left /
   real-video-panel-right, matching that reference's actual proportions
   instead of keeping the video as a small decorative extra. Video is
   stock footage, cropped from a portrait source to this landscape frame
   (verified across the whole clip that both people stay in frame, not
   just the first frame) and stripped of audio — ambient only, autoplay +
   loop + muted, no sound anywhere on this page. #}
<section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-paper py-section-sm border-b border-rule">
  {# 2026-09-06 correction: reverted to the ORIGINAL two-column layout
     (text | "what's changing" list) with the media element positioned
     exactly where the globe used to sit — same absolute slot, same size,
     same xl:block-only visibility. An earlier pass restructured this into
     a full-width video-panel layout, which was the wrong call: the actual
     ask was "keep this section's presentation exactly as it is, just
     swap the globe for the video" — not a layout rebuild. #}
  {# Same right-side slot/size the globe occupied (450px square footprint,
     xl:block only), but NOT forced into the globe's circular mask — a
     landscape video of two people cropped into a circle would cut off
     faces/chins unpredictably as object-cover centers within a square.
     Kept as a real rectangle instead, vertically centered in that same
     450px-tall footprint, which is what "same presentation" should
     actually mean for video content rather than literal shape-matching. #}
  <div class="absolute right-8 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 w-[450px] h-[450px] hidden xl:flex items-center" aria-hidden="true">
    {# Video, muted + looping, no controls needed for a 2.7s ambient loop.
       Cropped from a portrait source to 16:9, verified across the whole
       clip (not just one frame) that both people stay fully in shot.
       NOT the `autoplay` HTML attribute — that starts playback before any
       JS (including the reduced-motion check every other animation on
       this site respects) can run; this inline, synchronous script gates
       playback on prefers-reduced-motion the same way main.js never even
       loads cobe for those visitors. #}
    <video
      id="shift-video"
      class="w-full aspect-video object-cover bg-navy-deep shadow-raised"
      src="/assets/video/the-shift-team.mp4"
      poster="/assets/images/homepage/the-shift-poster.jpg"
      loop muted playsinline
    ></video>
  </div>
  <script>
    if (!window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) {
      var __shiftVideo = document.getElementById('shift-video');
      if (__shiftVideo) __shiftVideo.play();
    }
  </script>

  <div class="shell relative z-10 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,26rem)_minmax(0,15.5rem)] gap-x-12 gap-y-8 md:items-center">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow fade-up">The Shift</span>
      {# Was a <p> — this is the section's actual heading (h1 above, h3s
         below in the "what's changing" breakdown), so it was skipping
         straight from h1 to h3 with no h2 in between. Promoted to h2 with
         no class changes, so the visual size/weight is unchanged. #}
      <h2 class="mt-3 fade-up font-display font-light text-[clamp(1.5rem,1.1rem+1.8vw,2.3rem)] leading-[1.15] text-ink max-w-[20ch] text-balance" style="animation-delay:60ms">
        Education is more global. Careers are less linear. The skills a job needs can shift <em class="italic text-navy font-book">faster</em> than a degree can be finished.
      </h2>
      <span class="block mt-5 w-10 h-px bg-gold" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      {# Was text-small (13px) -- every sibling section-intro paragraph on
         this page (hero, "What Admizz Is", etc.) uses text-body-lg for this
         exact role; this one was the inconsistent outlier, which is why it
         read as "not visible properly" next to the huge heading above it.
         Matched to the sitewide convention instead of one-off darkening,
         which would have made it inconsistent in the other direction (every
         sibling keeps text-ink-muted, not full ink, at this larger size). #}
      <p class="mt-4 text-body-lg text-ink-muted max-w-[36ch] fade-up" style="animation-delay:120ms">
        For most people, the constraint isn&rsquo;t access anymore &mdash; it&rsquo;s knowing what comes next, and having a real way to prepare for it.
        Admizz operates across the three places that question actually gets answered: preparation, education, and work.
      </p>
      {# Was #what-admizz-is -- that section is now ABOVE this one (see the
         2026-09-02 note on this section's own header comment), so the old
         target would scroll backward up the page. Repointed to the
         Ecosystem/ventures section further down instead, keeping this a
         genuine "keep scrolling to learn more" link. #}
      <a href="#ventures" class="mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-small font-medium text-navy fade-up" style="animation-delay:170ms">
        Explore how we help
        <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 7h10M8 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
      </a>
    </div>

    {# The "what's changing" breakdown — three one-line elaborations of the
       headline statement above, not new claims about Admizz itself.
       Dividers between items are a dotted rule (border-dotted), matching
       the reference exactly — NOT the solid .border-rule hairline used
       everywhere else on this page. #}
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 fade-up" style="animation-delay:100ms">
      {% set shifts = [
        { title: "Education is changing.", text: "More options, more destinations, more complexity." },
        { title: "Careers are changing.", text: "Paths aren't fixed anymore. People move, pivot and grow." },
        { title: "Skills are changing.", text: "What you learn today may not be enough tomorrow." }
      ] %}
      {% for s in shifts %}
      <div class="flex gap-3 pt-4 border-t border-dotted border-ink-faint/50 first:pt-0 first:border-t-0">
        <span class="font-mono text-label tabular-nums text-navy-soft shrink-0">0{{ loop.index }}</span>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-display font-book text-body text-ink">{{ s.title }}</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-small text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">{{ s.text }}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ============================================================ THE ECOSYSTEM (register)
   The former standalone "Statement" section (its own eyebrow+headline+paragraph
   module) was cut here, not relocated — on inspection its copy was a near-verbatim
   restatement of the hero subhead above, with the "three pillars" line it added
   already covered more concretely by the venture-name ticker (real names, not
   category words) and by this register, which explains all three ventures in full. #}
{# No overflow-hidden here, deliberately — it silently breaks position:sticky
   on any descendant (an ancestor's overflow other than visible forces sticky
   to compute against that ancestor instead of the viewport), which is
   exactly what happened the first time this was written: the sticky photo
   below just scrolled away instead of staying put. #}
<section id="ventures" class="bg-paper py-section">
  <div class="shell">
    {# Subtitle stacked directly under the heading, not split off to the far
       right of the shell — that put real distance between a line and the
       heading it supports, reading as orphaned rather than connected. #}
    <div class="max-w-[42rem] fade-up">
      <span class="eyebrow">Prepare / Study / Work</span>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-display font-light text-h2 text-ink">Three businesses. Real ground covered.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-body-lg text-ink-muted max-w-measure-tight">
        Each of the three below solves a different problem, for a different audience &mdash; not three steps of one script.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  {# Deliberately outside .shell — the sticky-photo/text grid inside this
     partial breaks full-bleed to the viewport edge on its photo side. #}
  {% include "partials/ecosystem-journey.njk" %}
</section>

{# ============================================================ 04 — OUR EXPERTISE
   Rebuilt 2026-09-01 (was a click-to-expand row accordion, see git history
   for that version). Now 4 photo cards that flip to a description panel on
   hover — desktop only, since that's a real hover gesture; touch devices
   tap instead, detected via matchMedia('(hover: none)') inside Alpine
   rather than assuming touch = mobile width. Reuses the exact preview
   photos already downloaded for the ventures section above (institute/
   education/workforce-preview.jpg) — no new images sourced. Four
   categories, not six: verified against ventures.json's actual
   descriptions — test prep, admissions counseling, visa/scholarship
   support, and workforce development are the only capabilities with real
   copy behind them anywhere in this repo. Admissions & Counseling and
   Visa & Scholarship Support both sit under Admizz Education, so they
   share education-preview.jpg — the same grouping the venture data itself
   uses, not a mismatch. Career Development and Learning & Training (from
   the brief's example list) are still NOT included — no distinct,
   verifiable service exists for either beyond what Workforce Development
   already covers. #}
<section class="bg-paper py-section-sm md:py-section border-t border-rule">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="max-w-[42rem] fade-up">
      <span class="eyebrow">Our Expertise</span>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-display font-light text-h2 text-ink">What Admizz actually does.</h2>
    </div>

    {# Card-specific portrait photos (2026-09-01) — one distinct photo per
       expertise category rather than sharing the 3 venture-level photos
       used elsewhere on the page. User-supplied AI-generated images (same
       exception basis as preview/*.jpg and ecosystem/*.jpg above — see
       those comments), chosen/regenerated specifically for this card's
       native 3:4 portrait aspect (source is 1086x1448, exact 3:4) so
       object-cover needs no meaningful crop. Keyed by expertise index, not
       ventureId, since 02/03 both belong to Admizz Education but now get
       their own distinct photo instead of sharing one. #}
    {% set expertisePhotos = {
      "01": { file: "expertise/test-preparation.jpg", alt: "A student wearing headphones studying at a desk covered in handwritten notes and practice papers" },
      "02": { file: "expertise/admissions-counseling.jpg", alt: "A counselor pointing at a university shortlist on a laptop while a student looks on, passport on the table" },
      "03": { file: "expertise/visa-scholarship.jpg", alt: "A student reviewing a scholarship award letter and a visa application, passport on the desk" },
      "04": { file: "expertise/workforce-development.jpg", alt: "A job coach and a colleague using a wheelchair reviewing a resume together at an office table" }
    } %}
    {% set expertise = [
      { index: "01", name: "Test Preparation", ventureId: "institute", venture: "Admizz Institute", text: "Structured preparation for IELTS, PTE, SAT, GRE and GMAT — the tests that determine what an application can achieve before it's even submitted." },
      { index: "02", name: "Admissions & Counseling", ventureId: "education", venture: "Admizz Education", text: "Choosing a destination, shortlisting institutions, and building an application around a student's actual academic profile, not a template." },
      { index: "03", name: "Visa & Scholarship Support", ventureId: "education", venture: "Admizz Education", text: "Guidance through visa applications and scholarship opportunities — the practical steps that stand between an offer and actually enrolling." },
      { index: "04", name: "Workforce Development", ventureId: "workforce", venture: "Admizz Workforce Solutions", text: "Supported employment, job coaching and career-transition guidance, focused on vocational rehabilitation for individuals with disabilities." }
    ] %}
    <div class="expertise-grid mt-10 md:mt-12 fade-up" style="animation-delay:90ms">
      {% for e in expertise %}
      {% set img = expertisePhotos[e.index] %}
      {# 2026-09-06: replaced the hover/tap flip (photo face <-> separate
         opaque panel) with a single static face — reference: SaleUnion's
         case-study cards, where badge/heading/description/CTA all sit
         directly over the photo, always visible, nothing hidden behind an
         interaction. Badge position and index/name are untouched; the
         description and CTA (previously only reachable via the flip) now
         live in the same footer, over a deepened scrim so the extra text
         stays readable against the photo. Alpine touch-detection is gone
         with the flip it existed to support. #}
      <a href="/ventures/#record-{{ e.ventureId }}" class="expertise-card group">
        <div class="absolute inset-0 transition-transform duration-slow ease-signature group-hover:scale-105 [&_picture]:contents [&_picture]:block [&_picture]:h-full [&_img]:absolute [&_img]:inset-0 [&_img]:h-full [&_img]:w-full [&_img]:object-cover">
          {% image "src/assets/images/" + img.file, img.alt, "(min-width: 1024px) 25vw, (min-width: 640px) 45vw, 90vw" %}
        </div>
        <div class="expertise-card-scrim" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <span class="expertise-card-badge">{{ e.venture }}</span>
        <div class="expertise-card-footer">
          <span class="font-mono text-small tabular-nums text-navy-on-muted">{{ e.index }}</span>
          <h3 class="mt-1 font-display font-light text-h4 text-navy-on text-balance">{{ e.name }}</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-small text-navy-on-muted leading-relaxed">{{ e.text }}</p>
          <span class="btn-card-on-navy mt-3">
            Learn more
            <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 7h10M8 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          </span>
        </div>
      </a>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ============================================================ 05 — VENTURES COVERFLOW
   2026-09-02: removed the "Ecosystem pathway" diagram (Potential ->
   Preparation -> Education -> Skills -> Work -> Opportunity) that used to
   sit here, on user direction after a design critique flagged the same
   three ventures being told four times in a row before the footer (preview
   cards above -> the sticky "ecosystem-journey" record -> this pathway
   diagram -> this coverflow). The pathway and the coverflow covered nearly
   identical ground; this one survives because dropping the pathway (navy)
   instead of the coverflow (paper) keeps the paper/navy section rhythm
   intact — removing the coverflow instead would have put this section's
   navy neighbors (the stat band above / "What We Believe" below) directly
   back-to-back, the exact "too much blue" problem already fixed once
   before (see the coverflow comment below). If this trade doesn't read
   well in practice, the removed pathway markup is recoverable from git
   history (redesign/homepage-narrative branch, commit before 2026-09-02).

   Original 2026-08-31 note on this section, still accurate: adapted from a
   React/shadcn coverflow-carousel component (drag-to-browse, 3D
   perspective tilt on off-center cards). This site has no React — ported
   only the actual mechanics (pointer-drag tracking, velocity-based flick,
   the per-card 3D transform math, a requestAnimationFrame easing settle,
   keyboard arrow nav) into vanilla JS (main.js, guarded by
   `[data-coverflow]`).

   Content: the same 3 real venture photos already used elsewhere on this
   page (institute/education/workforce-preview.jpg), captioned with each
   venture's real name/stage/verticalLine — NOT the source component's demo
   content, which used random stock photos captioned with entirely
   fabricated "album" metadata (Producer, Length, Year).

   Only 3 real slides exist, fewer than this component pattern is usually
   built for — loop math still works correctly at any count, verified.

   2026-09-02: hidden on explicit request, same "if false" wrapper pattern
   already used elsewhere on this page (see "Our Story" section
   history) to disable a section without deleting it. The paper/navy
   rhythm concern in the note above no longer applies to hiding THIS
   section specifically — the section directly above (Our Expertise) is
   paper, and the section below (What We Believe) is navy, so removing
   this one just leaves a normal paper-to-navy transition, not two navy
   sections back to back. Re-enable by removing this wrapper. #}
{% if false %}
<section class="bg-paper pt-section-sm pb-10 md:pb-12 border-b border-rule">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="max-w-[42rem] fade-up">
      <span class="eyebrow">Our Ventures, Up Close</span>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-display font-light text-h2 text-ink">Drag or scroll through the three.</h2>
    </div>
  </div>

  {% set coverflowImages = {
    "institute": { file: "preview/institute-preview.jpg", alt: "Student wearing headphones, writing in a notebook" },
    "education": { file: "preview/education-preview.jpg", alt: "Student walking outside a university building with a backpack" },
    "workforce": { file: "preview/workforce-preview.jpg", alt: "Three colleagues talking in a modern office" }
  } %}
  <div class="coverflow mt-12 md:mt-16 fade-up" data-coverflow style="animation-delay:90ms; --cf-card: clamp(180px, 30vw, 340px);">
    <div class="coverflow-frame" data-coverflow-frame tabindex="0" role="region" aria-roledescription="carousel" aria-label="Admizz ventures">
      <div class="coverflow-track" data-coverflow-track>
        {% for v in ventures %}
        {% set img = coverflowImages[v.id] %}
        <div class="coverflow-card" data-coverflow-card role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" aria-label="{{ loop.index }} of {{ ventures.length }}">
          <div class="[&_picture]:contents [&_img]:absolute [&_img]:inset-0 [&_img]:h-full [&_img]:w-full [&_img]:object-cover">
            {% image "src/assets/images/" + img.file, img.alt, "340px" %}
          </div>
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="coverflow-hint mt-4 text-center font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-faint" data-coverflow-hint aria-hidden="true">Drag or scroll to explore</p>
  </div>

  <div class="shell mt-4">
    <div class="text-center" data-coverflow-caption>
      {% for v in ventures %}
      <div class="coverflow-caption-item {{ '' if loop.index0 == 0 else 'hidden' }}" data-coverflow-caption-item data-index="{{ loop.index0 }}">
        <span class="font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-navy-soft">{{ v.stage }} &middot; {{ v.vertical }}</span>
        <h3 class="mt-1.5 font-display font-book text-h4 text-ink">{{ v.name }}</h3>
        <p class="mt-1.5 text-small text-ink-muted max-w-[38ch] mx-auto">{{ v.verticalLine }}</p>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <div class="coverflow-dots mt-5 flex items-center justify-center gap-2.5" data-coverflow-dots role="tablist" aria-label="Choose a venture">
      {% for v in ventures %}
      <button
        type="button"
        class="coverflow-dot {{ 'is-active' if loop.index0 == 0 }}"
        data-coverflow-dot
        data-index="{{ loop.index0 }}"
        role="tab"
        aria-selected="{{ 'true' if loop.index0 == 0 else 'false' }}"
        aria-label="Show {{ v.name }}"
      ></button>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{% endif %}

{# ============================================================ 06 — WHAT WE BELIEVE
   Revived and rewritten from the disabled "Statement band" (previously
   wrapped in {% if false %}, hidden 2026-08-25). Same navy-band visual
   language, new job: a real point of view, not a generic mission quote.
   Three concise principles, each one sentence — deliberately not slogans
   ("unlock your potential" etc, banned by the brief). Grounded in what's
   already established across ventures.json/marketContext.json, not new
   claims.

   2026-08-31 v2: was an equal 3-column grid — the exact "sameness" pattern
   flagged as flat/templated. Reworked into an asymmetric 5/7-column split:
   principle 01 gets a raised, larger panel of its own (the one this project
   treats as foundational — everything else follows from taking preparation
   seriously); 02 and 03 stack smaller beside it. Grain texture replaces the
   section's previous plain gradient-only surface. #}
<section class="beliefs-section relative overflow-hidden bg-navy-deep py-section-sm">
  {% include "partials/grain-texture.njk" %}
  <div class="beliefs-glow absolute -bottom-1/3 -right-1/4 w-[70%] h-[200%] bg-gradient-to-tl from-navy-accent/40 via-navy-soft/15 to-transparent -rotate-12 blur-3xl pointer-events-none" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="shell relative">
    <span class="eyebrow-on-navy fade-up">What We Believe</span>
    {# Stacked-deck idle state (2026-09-01): 02/03 sit visually pulled back
       on top of 01's box via `transform` only — grid placement never
       changes, so the fan-out on hover is a pure transform transition,
       never a layout jump. Desktop/tablet (>=768px) only; mobile has no
       hover, so it stays the plain flat stack (main.css gates this behind
       a min-width media query). #}
    {# 2026-09-06: added an icon-in-circle badge per belief (reference:
       SaleUnion's icon-badge trust-pillar row) and lightened the panel's
       resting-state chrome (was a constant tinted background + visible
       border even at rest — now that only appears on hover, so the panel
       reads closer to SaleUnion's plain/minimal look by default). The
       asymmetric layout, stacked-deck cascade, hover fan-out and per-panel
       hover lift are all UNCHANGED — this is a skin change on top of the
       existing interaction, not a rebuild of it. Icons are chosen to match
       what each belief actually says, not decorative filler: a target for
       "not a formality" (precision), a trajectory arrow for "lead
       somewhere," and two overlapping rings for "close gaps." #}
    <div class="beliefs-stack mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-6 md:gap-8 items-start">
      <div class="belief-panel belief-panel-featured md:col-span-5 fade-up" style="animation-delay:80ms">
        <span class="belief-icon">
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 18 18" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="9" cy="9" r="7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4"/>
            <circle cx="9" cy="9" r="3.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4"/>
            <circle cx="9" cy="9" r="0.75" fill="currentColor"/>
          </svg>
        </span>
        <span class="block mt-4 font-mono text-small tabular-nums text-navy-accent">01</span>
        <h3 class="mt-2 font-display font-light text-h2 text-navy-on max-w-[14ch] text-balance">Preparation is not a formality.</h3>
        <p class="mt-4 text-body text-navy-on-muted leading-relaxed max-w-[34ch]">A test score or an application isn&rsquo;t a checkbox &mdash; it&rsquo;s the thing that decides which doors are actually open.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="md:col-span-7 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6 md:gap-8 md:mt-10">
        {% set beliefs = [
          { title: "Education should lead somewhere.", text: "A university choice is a career decision made early. We treat it as one, not as an admissions transaction.", icon: '<path d="M4 14L14 4M14 4H6M14 4V12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>' },
          { title: "Skills close gaps services alone don't.", text: "Access to a program is a start. What a person can actually do with it afterward is the part that's easy to overlook.", icon: '<circle cx="6.5" cy="9" r="4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4"/><circle cx="11.5" cy="9" r="4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4"/>' }
        ] %}
        {% for b in beliefs %}
        <div class="belief-panel belief-panel-stack-{{ loop.index }} fade-up" style="animation-delay:{{ loop.index0 * 90 + 170 }}ms">
          <span class="belief-icon">
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 18 18" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">{{ b.icon | safe }}</svg>
          </span>
          <span class="block mt-3 font-mono text-small tabular-nums text-navy-accent">0{{ loop.index + 1 }}</span>
          <h3 class="mt-2 font-display font-light text-h3 text-navy-on max-w-[16ch] text-balance">{{ b.title }}</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-small text-navy-on-muted leading-relaxed max-w-[32ch]">{{ b.text }}</p>
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

