{# ============================================================ INSIGHTS
   Photo-anchored editorial index. An earlier pass this session went
   text-only here, reasoning the 3 real Admizz-branded photos would read
   as stock at this size — reversed after actually looking at them again;
   they hold up fine, and every other homepage section is photo-anchored,
   so a text-only Insights block was the odd one out. Reuses the same
   rounded-lg/bg-navy-deep thumbnail pattern already proven on /insights/,
   not a new one. Reading time computed from real word count (readingTime
   filter, .eleventy.js). 3 real posts, presented as 3 — no invented 4th.

   Post 1's photo (study-abroad.jpg) is licensed Pexels stock, not an
   Admizz original — see insights.json's imageSource field for the exact
   license/reasoning. The original global-opportunities.jpg (still the
   homepage hero photo, untouched, see the hero section above) was ALSO
   this post's thumbnail, so it appeared twice on the same page scroll.
   Swapped this one usage rather than the hero, since the hero has much
   heavier bespoke art direction (parallax target, tuned crop, brand-shape
   overlay) built around that specific file. Same content-authenticity
   exception pattern as education.jpg/workforce.jpg in ecosystem-journey.njk
   — a deliberate, flagged substitution, not a new default. #}
<section class="bg-paper py-section-sm md:py-section">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-end md:justify-between gap-4 mb-10 fade-up">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Insights</span>
        <h2 class="mt-3 font-display font-light text-h2 text-ink">Ideas shaping what's next.</h2>
      </div>
      <a href="/insights/" class="text-small font-medium text-ink link-underline shrink-0">View all insights</a>
    </div>

    {# 2026-08-31 v2: was an equal 3-column grid (the same sameness problem
       as Beliefs) — reworked into a featured + rest layout using the
       `featured` field that's existed in insights.json since it was first
       written, unused until now. Featured post gets a wider 16:9 plate and
       runs the width of its column; the other two stack in a narrower,
       smaller-image column beside it — genuine editorial hierarchy, not
       three identical tiles. #}
    {% set featuredPost = insights | selectattr("featured") | first %}
    {% set restPosts = insights | rejectattr("featured") %}
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1.4fr)_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-x-10 gap-y-12">
      {% if featuredPost %}
      <article class="group fade-up">
        <a href="/insights/{{ featuredPost.slug }}/" class="block relative overflow-hidden bg-navy-deep aspect-[16/10]" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="absolute inset-0 transition-transform duration-slow ease-signature group-hover:scale-105 [&_picture]:block [&_picture]:h-full [&_img]:block [&_img]:h-full [&_img]:w-full [&_img]:object-cover">
            {% image "src/assets/images/insights/" + featuredPost.image, featuredPost.imageAlt, "(min-width: 1024px) 56vw, 100vw" %}
          </div>
          <span class="absolute inset-x-0 bottom-0 h-24 bg-gradient-to-t from-navy-deep/85 to-transparent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="absolute bottom-4 left-5 flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-white">
            <span class="w-4 h-px bg-gold" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            Featured
          </span>
        </a>
        <span class="mt-5 block font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-navy-soft">{{ featuredPost.venture }} &middot; {{ featuredPost.body | readingTime }} min read</span>
        <h3 class="mt-2 font-display font-light text-h2 text-ink text-balance max-w-[20ch]">
          <a href="/insights/{{ featuredPost.slug }}/" class="group-hover:text-navy-soft transition-colors duration-press ease-signature">{{ featuredPost.title }}</a>
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-body text-ink-muted max-w-measure-tight">{{ featuredPost.deck }}</p>
        <a href="/insights/{{ featuredPost.slug }}/" class="mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-small font-medium text-ink link-underline">Read the piece</a>
      </article>
      {% endif %}

      {# self-start: without it, this column is a grid item in the outer
         2-col row and gets force-stretched to match the tall featured
         article's height (CSS Grid's `align-content: normal` computes to
         `stretch`) -- content then sits at the top of that oversized box,
         leaving a large dead gap between the two article rows. self-start
         stops the stretch at the source instead of just hiding its
         symptoms further down. #}
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-y-10 self-start">
        {% for post in restPosts %}
        {# items-start: without it, this flex row's default cross-axis
           stretch made the aspect-square thumbnail stretch to match its
           sibling column's height (itself force-stretched by the outer
           2-col grid matching the tall featured article) -- a square photo
           rendering as a tall narrow rectangle. items-start locks the
           thumbnail to its own natural square size regardless of how tall
           any ancestor gets. #}
        <article class="group flex items-start gap-5 fade-up" style="animation-delay:{{ loop.index0 * 90 + 90 }}ms">
          {# 2026-09-03: the object-position-right crop this comment used to
             describe is gone -- two of the three source images
             (lifelong-learning.jpg, exams.jpg) had an Admizz logo watermark
             baked into a corner, and a 16/10 or square crop biased toward
             one edge still left a sliver of it visible at every aspect
             ratio these photos render at across the site (measured, not
             assumed). Fixed at the source instead: both files were cropped
             with sharp to physically remove the watermarked region, so a
             plain centered object-cover is correct here again. #}
          <a href="/insights/{{ post.slug }}/" class="block relative overflow-hidden bg-navy-deep aspect-square w-28 md:w-32 shrink-0" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="absolute inset-0 transition-transform duration-slow ease-signature group-hover:scale-105 [&_picture]:block [&_picture]:h-full [&_img]:block [&_img]:h-full [&_img]:w-full [&_img]:object-cover">
              {% image "src/assets/images/insights/" + post.image, post.imageAlt, "128px" %}
            </div>
          </a>
          <div class="min-w-0">
            <span class="block font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-navy-soft">{{ post.venture }} &middot; {{ post.body | readingTime }} min read</span>
            <h3 class="mt-1.5 font-display font-book text-h4 text-ink text-balance">
              <a href="/insights/{{ post.slug }}/" class="group-hover:text-navy-soft transition-colors duration-press ease-signature">{{ post.title }}</a>
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-small text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">{{ post.deck }}</p>
            <a href="/insights/{{ post.slug }}/" class="mt-3 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-small font-medium text-ink link-underline">Read the piece</a>
          </div>
        </article>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ============================================================ STATEMENT BAND
   Moved below Insights (was between the ecosystem section and "Our Story")
   on request — same section, same markup, just repositioned in the page.
   Hidden 2026-08-25 on request — wrapped in {% if false %} rather than
   deleted so it's a one-line revert, not a rebuild, if it comes back. #}
{% if false %}
<section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-navy py-section-sm">
  {# Ambient glow — same blurred-gradient technique as the hero value band's
     light sweep, a fresh instance (not the reserved .facet-field texture,
     which a code comment explicitly restricts to the hero+close "bookend"
     sections only — "not decoration sprinkled everywhere"). #}
  <div class="absolute -bottom-1/3 -right-1/4 w-[70%] h-[200%] bg-gradient-to-tl from-navy-accent/40 via-navy-soft/15 to-transparent -rotate-12 blur-3xl pointer-events-none" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <div class="shell relative">
    {# max-w was 18ch at up-to-64px text-display-2 — an 18-character column
       forced this ~115-character quote across 5-6 towering lines, which is
       the entire reason this band ballooned to ~2 viewport-heights of solid
       navy with empty space beside it. Widened to 42ch (→ 3 balanced lines)
       and stepped the size down to text-h1 (which brings its own tighter
       1.08 line-height/tracking, replacing the separate leading-tight) —
       a wider column at the old 64px would just trade one oversized axis
       for another.

       Split into phrase spans (not literal words — a fussy word-by-word
       reveal reads gimmicky) so main.js can stagger them in as the section
       scrolls into view, same duration/stagger feel as the hero entrance,
       just ScrollTrigger-gated instead of firing on load. Inline-block, not
       block, so the phrases still wrap naturally at any viewport instead of
       forcing hard line breaks at these split points. #}
    <p class="font-display font-light text-h1 text-navy-on max-w-[42ch] text-balance">
      <span class="statement-line inline-block">From vision to reality,</span>
      <span class="statement-line inline-block italic text-navy-accent font-book">shaping futures</span>
      <span class="statement-line inline-block">through innovation, collaboration,</span>
      <span class="statement-line inline-block">and a commitment to quality education.</span>
    </p>
    <span class="statement-line inline-block mt-8 md:block font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-navy-on-muted">&mdash; Admizz Group</span>
  </div>
</section>
{% endif %}

{# ============================================================ CLOSE
   2026-09-01 v2: first pass full-bleed photo was broken two ways — the
   overlay gradient direction was backwards, AND admissions-counseling.jpg's
   portrait 3:4 crop went nearly unrecognizable stretched across this
   section's ultra-wide band. Fixed at the time by confining the photo to a
   narrower right-hand panel instead.

   2026-09-06 v5: v4 matched the layout logic (centered, one column) but
   still used a heavier overlay and kept the facet-field texture, neither
   of which the reference actually has — a closer crop of the live
   SaleUnion site shows almost NO dark wash at all (their photo sits at
   close to full natural exposure) and zero texture on top of the photo.
   Can't copy "zero overlay" literally though: their heading is set BOLD,
   ours is font-light by sitewide convention (base.njk/type system, not
   specific to this section) — a thin stroke needs more contrast support
   than a thick one, so this keeps a light top-down wash (much reduced
   from v4) rather than none. facet-field is dropped on THIS section only
   (still present on the hero) to get the reference's clean-photo feel —
   a deliberate one-off exception to the "bookend pair" pattern, not a
   removal of the motif itself. #}
<section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-navy-deep py-section">
  {# Overscanned (-3% top/bottom) wrapper, same technique as .hero-photo-parallax
     and .facet-field — GSAP drifts this within the section's own static,
     overflow-hidden bounds so scrolling never exposes a gap. The section
     itself provides the fixed-size clipping layer here (unlike the hero,
     which needed its own inner overflow-hidden div, since this photo already
     spans the whole section rather than a sub-region of it). #}
  <div class="close-photo-parallax absolute -inset-y-[12%] inset-x-0 [&_picture]:contents [&_picture]:block [&_picture]:h-full [&_img]:absolute [&_img]:inset-0 [&_img]:h-full [&_img]:w-full [&_img]:object-cover [&_img]:object-[50%_15%] [&_img]:grayscale">
    {% image "src/assets/images/expertise/admissions-counseling.jpg", "A counselor and student in conversation", "100vw" %}
  </div>
  <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-b from-navy-deep/55 from-0% via-navy-deep/18 via-42% to-transparent to-75%"></div>
  <div class="shell relative text-center max-w-2xl mx-auto">
    <span class="eyebrow-on-navy fade-up">Get in touch</span>
    <h2 class="mt-4 font-display font-light text-display-2 text-navy-on max-w-[16ch] mx-auto text-balance fade-up" style="animation-delay:80ms">
      Let's talk about <em class="italic text-navy-accent font-book">what's next.</em>
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-5 text-body-lg text-navy-on-muted max-w-[38ch] mx-auto fade-up" style="animation-delay:120ms">
      Whether you're a student weighing options, an institution exploring partnership, or an organization building workforce capability &mdash; tell us which, and we'll route it to the right team.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-center gap-3 fade-up" style="animation-delay:160ms">
      <a href="/contact/" class="btn-primary w-full sm:w-auto text-center">Get in touch</a>
      <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}" class="btn-ghost-on-navy w-full sm:w-auto text-center">{{ site.email }}</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
